  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>The disputed figures</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Sama said that its workers had to read about 70 passages per shift.
One worker told the Guardian he read up to 700 a day.
Let's assume here that a shift is one day.</p>
<p>Suppose a worker does {@wk@} shifts in a week.
How many <em>more</em> passages would that worker read in the week if the worker's figure is right than if Sama's figure is right?
[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>With Sama's figure, the worker reads 70 &times; {@wk@} = {@70*wk@} passages.
With the worker's figure, it's 700 &times; {@wk@} = {@700*wk@} passages.
The difference is {@ta@}.</p>
<p>We don't know which figure is right.
But the gap between them is huge, and it changes what we think of the work.
Whoever says which is right needs to show their evidence.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
